+# Points Table — how to fill the sheet
+
+The overall standings at `/points-table` are read from one tab in the same
+Google Sheet the tournaments come from. Nothing else needs changing: add the
+tab, put numbers in it, and the page updates within a minute.
+
+## Naming the tab
+
+Call the tab any one of:
+
+`Points` · `Points Table` · `Point Table` · `Standings` · `Overall Points` ·
+`Overall` · `Leaderboard` · `Medal Tally`
+
+## Layout
+
+One row per sport, one column per team. The first column is the sport.
+
+| Sport        | BMM | GG | RR | TT | Notes         |
+| ------------ | --- | -- | -- | -- | ------------- |
+| Cricket      | 10  | 6  | 4  | 8  |               |
+| Football     | 6   | 10 | 8  | 4  |               |
+| Table Tennis |     |    |    |    | Final pending |
+| Carrom       | 4   | 8  | 10 | 6  |               |
+
+Rules the parser follows:
+
+- **Team columns** can be headed with the code (`RR`), the full name
+  (`Red Raiders`) or both (`Red Raiders (RR)`). They may be in any order.
+- **Blank, `-`, `TBD`, `NA` or `Pending`** means "not scored yet" and shows as
+  a dash on the site. It is *not* counted as zero.
+- **Totals are calculated by the site**, down each column. If you keep your own
+  `Total` row it is ignored rather than double-counted, so it can stay.
+- **Extra rows are fine.** A `Bonus` or `Spirit Award` row is just another row
+  and adds into the totals like any sport.
+- **A `Notes` / `Status` / `Remarks` column** is shown as small grey text under
+  the sport name. Any other columns you keep for your own working are ignored.
+- **Sport names that match a tournament** (its slug, sport or name in the
+  `Tournaments` tab) become links to that tournament's page.
+
+### The sideways layout also works
+
+If it is easier to write teams down the side and sports across the top, do
+that instead — the parser detects which axis holds the team names:
+
+| Team | Cricket | Football | Carrom |
+| ---- | ------- | -------- | ------ |
+| BMM  | 10      | 6        | 4      |
+| GG   | 6       | 10       | 8      |
+
+## Before the sheet is ready
+
+With no points tab in the sheet, the page still renders: the four teams sit at
+a dash, and every published tournament gets a blank row. The site never invents
+a score.
+
+## Checking it
+
+`/api/sheet-status` lists every row the parser could not understand, e.g. a
+points cell holding text instead of a number.
